# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version ^2.0.1 using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
- Modified `app/[locale]/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Analytics
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, following Next.js App Router best practices

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide for Next.js App Router:
- The Analytics component was placed inside the root layout to track all pages
- The component is positioned after the main application content but still within the body tag
- This ensures analytics tracking is active across all routes and locales

## Files Modified

1. **webapp/package.json** - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. **webapp/package-lock.json** - Updated with new dependency lockfile information
3. **webapp/app/[locale]/layout.tsx** - Added Analytics import and component

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ Linter passed with no new errors (`npm run lint`)
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ No breaking changes introduced

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Verify analytics tracking by checking the Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

The analytics will automatically start collecting data once deployed to Vercel.
